      "blocked_reason": "REACHED AND CORRECT; BLOCKED ON THE composition_motif_search TRANSPORT STALL, and on a confirm token nothing confirms.\n\nTHE OLD REASON IS REFUTED. p4-confirm blocked this tool as 'an unanswerable prompt, and the model is right' — the prompt named no target. This scenario names the built-in trope 'Face-Slap Reversal' verbatim from the tool's own declared synonyms, and the model found it and adopted it: 2/5 runs ran composition_motif_search -> composition_motif_adopt with {motif_id: 92bfdcb0-58d1-5f03-ac65-dc5d3afb6f9f, target: 'user', book_id: <the run's book>} and got back ok:true with a well-formed confirm_token. Nothing about the tool or the prompt is the blocker.\n\n(1) LIVE clean fails 3/5: every failing run died with 'upstream sent \"error\" with no error message' immediately after composition_motif_search — the population already filed as D-THE-STALL-CONCENTRATES-ON-COMPOSITION-MOTIF-SEARCH. This tool cannot clear until that does, because search is its only supplier of the motif_id.\n\n(2) DATA cannot move: motif_adopt is two-phase and returns a confirm_token, so the store is CORRECTLY unchanged until something confirms it. The model's own closing line was 'please confirm the adoption in the card'. WHETHER A CARD REACHED THE FE IS UNVERIFIED HERE — the harness keeps CUSTOM event counts only, not their payloads, so this evidence cannot distinguish 'a card was emitted and nobody clicked it' from 'no card was emitted'. Recorded as unverified rather than as a missing-card defect; a scenario that confirms via the composition '?token=' convention would settle both.\n\nNote the store line reads 'unchanged' for a second reason too: adopted motifs are owner-scoped (motif.owner_user_id), and store_snapshot discovers book_id-carrying tables, so it is structurally blind to this tool's write. Verified directly against loreweave_composition.motif — no rows, consistent with the unconfirmed token."
